  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 352 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nMild temperatures prevail this afternoon with widespread upper 40s \nto low 50s. H5 ridge continues eastward into the Upper Mississippi \nValley and into the Ohio River Valley by late Monday. Troughing \nforms in western Wyoming late Tuesday, then deepens into an upper \nlow heading into Wednesday. Ensemble members still show variation in \nthe potential track; however, the majority of scenarios only bring \nlight rain into the area late Wednesday night into Thursday morning. \nBest chances for any measurable precip will be along and north of \nHighway 2. Cooler temperatures follow this system, bringing near \naverage to slightly above average temps into the Northern Plains and \nUpper Midwest through the end of the week and into the weekend. \n\nAnother potential system could bring precipitation back into the \narea late Friday through early Sunday. Cooler air will be in place, \nbut it is uncertain if we will have enough cold air in place to \nallow a mention of snow across some areas. Ensemble members show \nmultiple scenarios, with each dependent upon the track of the upper \nlow as it moves northeastward out of Colorado on Friday.",
